# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.xdv
*.nav
*.snm
*.bcf
*.run.xml
*.bbl
*.blg

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Python bytecode, left behind whenever a book's pagemap.py is imported by
# another script in the same directory
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor backups
*~
\#*\#
.\#*
scan.pdf

# Source scans kept locally for image-verified transcription. Large, and not
# ours to redistribute (public repo + GitHub Pages). NEVER commit these.
#   scan.pdf     — KB copy, shelfmark 14,-225 8°  (the working witness)
#   bodleian.pdf — Google Books scan of the Bodleian copy (the second witness,
#                  copied from ~/bibliotek/Nielsen, Rasmus/religion-1869.pdf)
bodleian.pdf

# Page renders used for image-verified transcription
.render/

# Tesseract language models, fetched per-machine for OCR of non-Danish sources
# (fra.traineddata for Høffding's French articles). Multi-megabyte binaries that
# are not ours and are trivially re-downloadable — never commit them.
.tessdata/

# Ebooks — privately owned copies kept alongside the texts for local
# searching only. NEVER commit/publish these (public repo + GitHub Pages).
# Note: transcription.pdf / translation.pdf are intentionally NOT ignored.
*.epub
*.mobi
*.azw
*.azw3
*.kfx
*.kepub
*.fb2

# Transcription-agent scratch: page renders and crops. These are regenerable from
# the scans in bibliotek/ and must never be committed — one batch put 25 MB of PNGs
# into the history.
.scratch-*/
**/.parts/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BOOK DIRECTORIES TRACK THE EDITION, NOTHING ELSE.
#
# A book directory under texts/<author>/<slug>/ should contain, in git, only the
# edition itself: transcription.tex / transcription.pdf / translation.tex /
# translation.pdf (plus the occasional toc.tex, transcription.md).
#
# EXCEPTION, texts/bohr/: both sides of that edition are transcriptions of
# published texts — the English volumes are Bohr's own published English, not a
# translation made here — so the files are transcription-da.tex and
# transcription-en.tex. Each volume also carries per-essay offprints under
# parts/<lang>/, which ARE part of the edition and are tracked. All of it is
# generated by bohr-edition/ at the repo root; edit the generator, not the
# output.
#
# Everything else there is production scaffolding — per-book harnesses, agent
# prompts, work logs, scratch. It is deliberately NOT tracked, for three reasons:
#   1. This repo is public and feeds GitHub Pages. A reader of the edition has no
#      use for a subagent prompt or a batch log.
#   2. The harnesses are unrunnable from a fresh clone anyway: they all depend on
#      the source scans in ~/bibliotek, which are correctly not in this repo. So
#      tracking them buys the appearance of reproducibility, not the substance.
#   3. They are near-duplicates from book to book, and they bloat the history.
#
# The durable scholarly record — the verified page map, the errata applied, the
# normalisation conventions, the logged printer's defects — belongs in the
# COMMENT HEADER of transcription.tex, where it travels with the edition.
# RESUME-NOTES.md stays on disk, untracked, as a working file.
texts/**/*.py
texts/**/*.sh
texts/**/BATCH-AGENT.md
texts/**/RESUME-NOTES.md
texts/**/RECON.md
# Per-pass recon fragments, written by subagents and concatenated into RECON.md.
# The sandbox cannot unlink files, so these survive the session that made them.
texts/**/.recon-*.md
texts/**/VERIFICATION.md
texts/**/TRANSLATION-RESUME-NOTES.md
texts/**/.gitignore

# Scratch and junk that has actually reached this history before
texts/**/*.png
texts/**/*.tmp
texts/**/*.bak.*
texts/**/.fuse_hidden*

# Source scans must never sit inside texts/ either. One did:
# texts/moller/udoedelighed/moller-udoedelighed-scan.pdf (3.9 MB).
texts/**/*-scan.pdf
texts/**/scan*.pdf

# Third-party corpora cloned locally for consultation, not part of this edition.
# Currently: _working/SKS_tei — the Royal Danish Library's TEI XML of Søren
# Kierkegaards Skrifter (github.com/kb-dk/SKS_tei, CC0), ~520 MB with its own
# .git. Nothing under _working/ should ever enter this repo's history.
_working/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EMBARGOED TEXTS — IN COPYRIGHT. DO NOT COMMIT, DO NOT PUBLISH.
#
# Added 2026-09-04. Everything else in this repo is public-domain
# nineteenth-century material; these three are not, and they are the first
# items here whose author's term has not run. Danish copyright is life + 70.
#
#   H. M. Hansen (1886 – 13 June 1956)   free 1 JANUARY 2027
#     texts/kroman/hansen-relativitetsprincipet/  (Fysisk Tidsskrift 10, 1912)
#     texts/kroman/hansen-svar/                   (Fysisk Tidsskrift 15, 1916)
#
#   C. E. Walsøe — RELEASED 2026-09-04. Identified as Carl Emil Walsøe,
#     b. 25 May 1870 Copenhagen, d. 1951, cand. polyt. 1896, district engineer
#     at Post- og Telegrafvæsenet. Public domain since 1 January 2022, so his
#     line has been removed from the list below.
#
# transcription.pdf is normally NOT ignored in this repo (see the block above);
# these entries deliberately override that, so the built PDF cannot reach
# GitHub Pages either. publish-danish.sh stages texts/, so without these lines
# a routine publish would put all three online.
#
# TO RELEASE: on 1 January 2027 delete the two Hansen lines, and delete this
# block once it is empty. NOTE that .gitignore does NOT cover files already
# tracked — both Hansen files were, and had to be `git rm --cached`ed first.
texts/kroman/hansen-relativitetsprincipet/transcription.*
texts/kroman/hansen-svar/transcription.*
